{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/215465-story-hooks-to-put-the-players-on-edge","id":215465,"title":"Story-hooks to put the players on edge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-31T20:09:43-07:00","id":215465,"title":"Story-hooks to put the players on edge","content":"Goose Chase/ Reds Under The Bed?:<br /> <br /> The ring has finally finished fighting through a grueling gauntlet against a large number of stigmatic cultists who have succeeded in summoning an angel not long before they arrived. Once they encounter said angel, it does the unexpected and surrenders immediately, allowing itself to be captured. The ring contacts their superiors within the Agency, who are just as baffled as they are, and are reluctantly ordered to bring the loyalist in for questioning. What is the angel's angle, is it's capture all part of the mission given to it? Complicating the matter further; things begin going haywire not long after the angel is detained: captured restoration facilities begin malfunctioning and inflicting glitches, several agents suffer serious damage to their Covers from seemingly innocuous events, and worst of all the Machine seems to examining demonic activities with greater scrutiny than it has in the past. Fingers are quickly pointed at the imprisoned angel as the culprit, but interrogation and periodic scans for aetheric resonance performed in it's presence when a incident is reported all reveal that the prisoner is innocent. If that is the case, what is causing all the disturbances around the city? Can the ring discover the true culprit before a horrible disaster happens? What does the ring do when their allies begin accusing each other of being undercover loyalists for the God-Machine?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Now that I have put this up here to kick things off, I'd be willing to see what sort of story-hooks you all would come up with to create a suspenseful game for the players. As always, I look forward to your responses!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T05:18:38-07:00","id":216659,"title":"","content":"Suddenly the Agency keeps on winning every fight agains the GM.<br /> Every single one.<br /> <br /> One of the responsibles for this change it was supposed to be a messenger, who was feeding the Agency with accurate information, but now the players discovered something terrible: he is not a fallen angel.<br /> <br /> Malachias is an old mortal capable of altering the reality in such deep form that could kill -or even create! - angels and he is fighting the GM for years, using demons as thugs and letting them suffer the consequences, always hiding in the shadows of this war.<br /> <br /> The players discovery that Malachias is worshipping &quot;things&quot; that were described in old books as dead Gods, awaiting in a sort of &quot;inferno&quot; to grow in power and take over reality. They just need to destroy GM, and the players are helping them to do so.<br /> <br /> Will they keep on fighting GM or will they, just for once, change sides and help GM to destroy one of his most feared enemies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T21:59:33-07:00","id":217175,"title":"","content":"An unchained with a law enforcement cover enters a murder scene at a private residence. Very quickly, she realizes that the houses is an exact copy of her own home, right down to the furnishings, books, toys etcetera. A quick check of the ol' perfect memory reveals that this home, this family, is an exact copy of what her own was, four years to the day. The schoolbooks her children were working on, the Dean Koontz book she was reading, the slain couple even had the exact same jobs the demon and her spouse had 4 years ago, with the same companies. <br /> <br /> Or rather, the house would have been an exact copy before it was ransacked. All four inhabitants were murder and brutally disfigured, even dental forensics will not be able to identify them. All the photos in home are also disfigured.<br /> <br /> Above the children's bed, the words &quot;<i>It hunts, but it does not live</i>&quot; are cut into the wall.<br /> <br /> Is the result of a cast off cover being reclaimed for the G-M's own purposes? A coincidence? A sick warning? Some sort of ploy by a malfunctioning hunter angel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}